# Module 1 – Governance and Compliance

## Governance
- Defines cybersecurity accountability
- Aligns security with business goals
- Helps manage cyber risks

## Important Roles

### Data Owner
- Responsible for data ownership and classification

### Data Custodian
- Maintains and protects systems storing data

### Data Protection Officer (DPO)
- Ensures privacy law compliance

## Cybersecurity Policies
- Password Policy
- Acceptable Use Policy (AUP)
- Remote Access Policy
- Incident Handling Policy

## Human Resources Security
- Security awareness training prevents phishing attacks
- User access controls enforce the need-to-know principle
- IDS/IPS monitoring detects unauthorized software downloads
- Monitoring abnormal employee behavior helps identify policy violations

## Key Takeaway
- Effective cybersecurity relies on governance, policies, and employee accountability to protect organizational data and systems.
